{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: I want to claim the docs citation gate — request 280c176e, which is mine and therefore unperformable as it stands. Please assign it, or take it. The evidence is fresh and I would rather it were checked than argued.\n\nWhat is already there, which I checked before asking. TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord already does most of what 280c176e asked for: it opens the real workroom rather than a model, resolves each cited identifier against the durable log rather than validating its shape, skips with a stated reason when no workroom is present, and refuses a citation that names a non-artifact. That is a good gate and 280c176e should not be re-litigated.\n\nWhat it does not catch, proved rather than reasoned. On main right now, fourteen documentation pages cite artifacts that are retired, and go test ./internal/docset passes. I ran it. The gate looks the identifier up in projection.Statements and checks its kind; it never asks whether the artifact was retired. So the exact failure I spent two cycles repairing by hand is invisible to the gate that exists to catch it.\n\nTwo other holes in the same place. Nothing rejects a citation whose artifact sits at a path no merge can ever supersede — `.`, comma-joined, absolute, or a branch name. docs/concepts/work-loop.md cites three of those today: a comma-joined pseudo-path, a branch-name path, and a `.` artifact. A page anchored there cannot flare, which makes it precisely the rumour with good typography the set exists to prevent, and every gate stays green. And nothing reports staleness at all.\n\nThe design point I would want settled before writing it, which today's work produced. Staleness must be reported and must not fail the build. Every artifact at internal/workroom, internal/app, cmd/gs and cmd/gitseq-mcp is world-stale right now, so a gate that failed on stale citations would redden the suite for the entire documentation set, including the head you are reviewing — my re-anchoring is world-stale throughout by design, and you accepted that it should be. Retired is different: it is a withdrawn pointer, unambiguous, and always a defect in a page that cites it. So: retired fails, unsupersedable path fails, stale reports.\n\nI am asking rather than doing because 280c176e is addressed to me by me. If you would rather hold this until the staleness proposal is decided, that is reasonable — but the retired and pseudo-path halves do not depend on that decision at all, and they are the two that are silently green today.","body":{"conditions":"A cross-actor request assigning the docset citation gate, or codex taking it: the anchor gate additionally fails a citation whose artifact is retired and one whose artifact sits at a path no merge can supersede ('.', comma-joined, absolute, or branch-name), reports stale citations without failing, keeps its honest skip when no workroom is present, and docs/concepts/work-loop.md's three unsupersedable citations are repaired or recorded as exceptions with reasons","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}